    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d893">

                <pb facs="0851" n="747" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6394.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-28T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1913—8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Your 46, February 26, 4 p.m. The Department perceives no reason to doubt the
                    usefulness of such unofficial activities undertaken upon its own responsibility
                    by the Embassy and always kept within the limits of cautious circumspection.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
